    "text": "Let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Total eggs laid per day**  \nJanet’s ducks lay **16 eggs per day**.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Eggs used for breakfast**  \nJanet eats **3 eggs for breakfast** every morning.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Eggs used for muffins**  \nShe uses **4 eggs** to bake muffins every day.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Total eggs used per day**  \n$$\n3 \\text{ (breakfast)} + 4 \\text{ (muffins)} = 7 \\text{ eggs}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Eggs remaining for sale**  \n$$\n16 \\text{ (total eggs)} - 7 \\text{ (used)} = 9 \\text{ eggs}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 6: Revenue from selling eggs**  \nShe sells the remaining eggs at **$2 per egg**.\n\n$$\n9 \\text{ eggs} \\times 2 \\text{ dollars per egg} = 18 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n#### <answer>18</answer>",
