    "text": "We are given the following relationships:\n\n1. **Toulouse has twice as many sheep as Charleston.**\n2. **Charleston has 4 times as many sheep as Seattle.**\n3. **Seattle has 20 sheep.**\n\nLet's solve this step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the number of sheep in Charleston\n\nWe are told:\n\n$$\n\\text{Charleston} = 4 \\times \\text{Seattle}\n$$\n\nSince Seattle has 20 sheep:\n\n$$\n\\text{Charleston} = 4 \\times 20 = 80\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the number of sheep in Toulouse\n\nWe are told:\n\n$$\n\\text{Toulouse} = 2 \\times \\text{Charleston}\n$$\n\nWe already found that Charleston has 80 sheep:\n\n$$\n\\text{Toulouse} = 2 \\times 80 = 160\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find the total number of sheep\n\nNow, add up the number of sheep in Toulouse, Charleston, and Seattle:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total} = \\text{Toulouse} + \\text{Charleston} + \\text{Seattle}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Total} = 160 + 80 + 20 = 260\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{260}\n$$\n\n#### <answer>260</answer>",
