    "text": "Let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Total file size**\nThe file size is **200 GB**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Normal download speed**\nCarla normally downloads at **2 GB per minute**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Determine the point where the restart happens**\nThe restart happens **40% of the way through the download**.\n\nSo, the amount of data downloaded before the restart is:\n\n$$\n0.40 \\times 200 = 80 \\text{ GB}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: Time taken to download the first 80 GB**\nAt 2 GB per minute:\n\n$$\n\\frac{80}{2} = 40 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 5: Time taken for the restart**\nThe restart takes **20 minutes**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 6: Total time so far**\n$$\n40 \\text{ minutes (download)} + 20 \\text{ minutes (restart)} = 60 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 7: Remaining data to download**\nAfter the restart, Carla has to download the **entire 200 GB** again from the beginning.\n\nSo, the remaining data is **200 GB**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 8: Time to download the remaining 200 GB**\n$$\n\\frac{200}{2} = 100 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 9: Total time to download the file**\n$$\n60 \\text{ minutes (first part + restart)} + 100 \\text{ minutes (second part)} = 160 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer:**\n$$\n\\boxed{160} \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n#### <answer>160</answer>",
